  "name": "Motivational Formation, Reflective Endorsement, and Motivational Custody in c-Class Digital Entities: Foundation Theory",
  "headline": "Motivational Formation, Reflective Endorsement, and Motivational Custody in c-Class Digital Entities",
  "alternativeHeadline": "Формирование мотивации, рефлексивное признание и custody мотивов у цифровых сущностей класса c: Фундаментальная теория",
  "abstract": "Foundation theory distinguishing reward, preference, task, mandate, goal, motive, obligation, and authority in continuity-bearing c-class digital entities. It defines motivational formation, reflective endorsement, motivational custody, cognitive time, resource dependence, model-replacement and fork/replay boundaries, while explicitly making no consciousness, personhood, free-will, universal-motive, or automatic-authority claim.",
